Let
\[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
x + 3 & \text{if $x < 20$}, \\
2x - 2 & \text{if $x \ge 20$}.
\end{array}
\right.\]Find $f^{-1}(7) + f^{-1}(46).$

What is the least number of colors needed to shade the following pattern, such that no two adjacent regions have the same color?

[asy]
for(int i=0;i<5;++i){
for(int j=0;j<5;++j){
filldraw(circle((i,j),0.4),white);
if(i<4 && j<4){
draw((i+0.4,j+0.4)--(i+1-0.4,j+0.4)--(i+1-0.4,j+1-0.4)--(i+0.4,j+1-0.4)--cycle);
}
}
}
[/asy]
